    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d197">

                <pb facs="0195" n="183" sameAs="frus:frus1941v01/pg183"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">741.6111/3: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Steinhardt</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-07-12T22:00:00+03:00">July 12, 1941—10
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received July 12—9:45 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1346. The British Ambassador informed me this evening that he signed the Pact of
                    Mutual Assistance and its supplementary provision precluding a separate peace
                    with Germany this afternoon at 5 o’clock at the Kremlin.<anchor n="57"
                        xml:id="d197-f1"/> Stalin was present at the signature.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Steinhardt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d197-f1" n="57" xml:id="d197-f1-content">
                <p>Agreement for Joint Action and Mutual Assistance; for text, see League of Nations
                    Treaty Series, vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps">cciv</hi>, p. 277; or Department
                    of State <hi rendition="#italic">Bulletin</hi>, September 27, 1941, p. 240.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
